<section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-white reveal">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">

      <!-- Photo -->
      <div class="flex justify-center lg:justify-start">
        <img src="/eric.jpg" alt="Eric" class="w-56 h-56 lg:w-72 lg:h-72 rounded-full object-cover shadow-xl" />
      </div>

      <!-- Text -->
      <div>
        <p class="text-marigold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">About Eric</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-navy tracking-tight mb-5">
          I've spent 4 years teaching <i>just</i> this one test.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Back in 2021, I scored a perfect 800 on the SAT Math both times I took it. 
            My goal as a tutor is to help other students do the same.
          </p>
          <p>
            Right now, I'm in my final year at the University of Virginia,
            studying Computer Science, Economics, and Math.
          </p>
          <p>
            As a lifelong student, I understand the pitfalls of education and have become deeply
            obsessed with the science behind learning. Most test prep is dry, outdated,
            and focused more on brute forcing problems than genuinely understanding them. 
            I hope to change that!
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
